    √ out of order: ball + want + i_me → request (deixis wins over position) (2 ms)
    √ subject-before-object among plain nouns; verb floats (cat + dog + chase) (2 ms)
    √ animacy overrides position: apple + i_me + eat = I eat the apple (4 ms)
    √ a state verb keeps the noun as object even reversed (apple + want) (1 ms)
    √ movement verb: you + follow + i_me → command, subject listener, destination me (2 ms)
    √ movement verb: you + go + there → command toward the gaze point (2 ms)
    √ gaze deixis: put + this + in + here (2 ms)
  rules — a condition connective makes a standing rule
    √ when + night + go + home → rule, while, action go home, condition night (2 ms)
    √ the reverse order parses identically: go + home + when + night (2 ms)
    √ if → edge, until → until (2 ms)
  word-order conformance — a teaching signal, not a gate
    √ well-ordered SVO scores 1 (no confusion) (2 ms)
    √ reversed order still PARSES but scores low (NPC shows confusion) (2 ms)
    √ only explicitly-placed roles count (implied subject isn't 'misordered') (2 ms)
